    - [38;5;153mgetCurrentUser()[39m returns [38;5;153m{ userId, username }[39m, or [38;5;153mnull[39m.
    - [38;5;153mgetCurrentUserId()[39m is a shortcut that returns just the ID, or [38;5;153mnull[39m.
    - [38;5;153mclearSession()[39m removes the saved user (for a future logout).
  - [1m[38;5;153mlogin(username, password)[39m in [38;5;153mapp.js[0m keeps its inputs and now returns [38;5;153m{ success, user, userId }[39m. The API is still a
    stub, so it returns a stand-in [38;5;153muserId[39m until the real endpoint exists. The stub will be clearly marked as such.
  - [1mThe submit handler[0m calls [38;5;153mSession.setCurrentUser(...)[39m only when [38;5;153mresult.success[39m is true. A failed login never writes
    anything.
  - [1mFuture forms[0m call [38;5;153mSession.getCurrentUserId()[39m and never read [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m directly, so the storage can be swapped
    later without touching them.

  Does this section look right? After it, I'll cover error handling (bad or unavailable storage, failed logins) and
  testing.

[38;5;246m✻[39m [38;5;246mCrunched for 44s · done 2:59 PM[39m

[38;5;246m[48;5;237m❯ [38;5;231mYes, that section looks right, continue.[39m

[38;5;231m[49m⏺[39m [1mSection 2: Error handling[0m

  - [1mStorage unavailable.[0m [38;5;153msessionStorage[39m can throw an error in some browser privacy modes or when storage is full. Each
    [38;5;153mSession[39m function catches that error, writes a [38;5;153mconsole.warn[39m, and keeps going. [38;5;153msetCurrentUser[39m does nothing, and both
    getters return [38;5;153mnull[39m. Login still succeeds; the user just isn't remembered after a reload.
  - [1mCorrupt or old stored value.[0m If [38;5;153m"currentUser"[39m doesn't parse as JSON or has no [38;5;153muserId[39m, [38;5;153mgetCurrentUser()[39m treats it as
    empty: it calls [38;5;153mclearSession()[39m and returns [38;5;153mnull[39m. Future forms only ever get a valid user or [38;5;153mnull[39m.
  - [1mBad input to [38;5;153msetCurrentUser[39m.[0m A missing or empty [38;5;153muserId[39m throws an error. That's a bug in the calling code, and we
    want it caught right away rather than saving an anonymous user.
  - [1mFailed login.[0m Nothing is written. Any user already saved from an earlier login stays as it is. A failed attempt
    doesn't log anyone out; logging out will be an explicit [38;5;153mclearSession()[39m.
  - [1mTrust boundary.[0m A code comment in [38;5;153msession.js[39m says the stored ID is for the browser side only. Servers must check who
    the user is themselves.

  Does this section look right? Next is testing. The repo has no test runner yet, so that section includes a question
  about what to set up.

